28
00:01:16,767 --> 00:01:17,733
But a number?

29
00:01:17,733 --> 00:01:20,033
That's the thing you do them to!

30
00:01:20,933 --> 00:01:23,400
Last one, question fifteen,

31
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:24,833
a number puzzle,

32
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:26,267
and it's sneaky!

33
00:01:26,267 --> 00:01:28,667
If four plus five makes twenty,

34
00:01:28,667 --> 00:01:30,967
three plus six makes eighteen,

35
00:01:30,967 --> 00:01:33,767
and two plus seven makes fourteen...

36
00:01:33,767 --> 00:01:36,567
then five plus four makes...

37
00:01:36,567 --> 00:01:38,967
what? A, nine...

38
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,300
B, eighteen... C,

39
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:42,900
twenty... or D,

40
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:45,333
twenty-five? Five seconds!

41
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:53,333
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

42
00:01:53,633 --> 00:01:55,100
The answer is...

43
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:57,533
C, twenty! Here's the trick:

44
00:01:57,533 --> 00:02:00,833
that plus sign secretly means multiply.

45
00:02:00,833 --> 00:02:02,633
Four times five is twenty,

46
00:02:02,633 --> 00:02:05,733
so five times four is twenty too!

47
00:02:06,767 --> 00:02:09,700
So, are you smart or fart?

48
